  "solution": "Given :\n\nI. 203 + 44 - 27 × 19 ÷ 11 = 114\n\nII. 9 × 572 ÷ 19 - 44 + 4 = 120\n\nAccording to the question, by interchanging the given two numbers i.e 44 and 19 :\n\nSo according to the BODMAS rule ;\n\nI. 203 + 19 - 27 × __**44 ÷ 11**__ = 114\n\n203 + 19 - __**27 × 4**__ = 114\n\n__**203 + 19**__ - 108 = 114\n\n__**222 - 108**__ = 114\n\n**114 = 114**** (LHS = RHS)**\n\nAnd,\n\nII. 9 × __**572 ÷ 44**__ - 19 + 4 = 120\n\n__**9 × 13**__ - 19 + 4 = 120\n\n**117** - 19 __**+ 4**__ = 120\n\n__**121 - 19**__ = 120\n\n**102 ≠ 120 (LHS ≠ RHS)**\n\n**⇒**Here, Only I is correct equation.\n\nHence, **\"Only I\"** is the correct answer.",
